    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const item = $input.item.json;\n\n// Read transaction fields\n// Handle both direct field names and possible variations\nconst transactionId   = item[\"TransactionID\"]   || item[\"transactionId\"]   || \"\";\nconst transactionDate = item[\"TransactionDate\"]  || item[\"transactionDate\"] || \"\";\nconst vendorName      = (item[\"VendorName\"]      || item[\"vendorName\"]      || \"\").trim();\nconst amount          = parseFloat(item[\"Amount\"] || item[\"amount\"] || 0);\nconst rawDescription  = (item[\"RawDescription\"]  || item[\"rawDescription\"]  || \"\").trim();\nconst currentLabel    = item[\"CurrentAccountLabel\"] || item[\"currentAccountLabel\"] || \"\";\nconst rowNumber       = item[\"row_number\"] || \"\";\n\n// Edge case 1: Missing or too-short description\nconst descriptionMissing =\n  !rawDescription ||\n  rawDescription.length < 3 ||\n  rawDescription.toLowerCase() === \"n/a\" ||\n  rawDescription.toLowerCase() === \"unknown\" ||\n  rawDescription.toLowerCase() === \"null\";\n\n// Edge case 2: Unusually large amount\n// Flag any transaction above $10,000 for mandatory audit\nconst LARGE_AMOUNT_THRESHOLD = 10000;\nconst isLargeAmount = Math.abs(amount) >= LARGE_AMOUNT_THRESHOLD;\n\n// Build audit flag string\nlet auditFlag = \"None\";\nif (descriptionMissing && isLargeAmount) {\n  auditFlag = \"Missing Description + Large Amount\";\n} else if (descriptionMissing) {\n  auditFlag = \"Missing Description\";\n} else if (isLargeAmount) {\n  auditFlag = \"Large Amount — Review Required\";\n}\n\n// Build the description the AI will see\n// If description is missing use vendor name only\nconst descriptionForAI = descriptionMissing\n  ? `Vendor: ${vendorName || \"Unknown vendor\"} — No description available`\n  : rawDescription;\n\nreturn {\n  transactionId,\n  transactionDate,\n  vendorName,\n  amount,\n  rawDescription,\n  descriptionForAI,\n  currentLabel,\n  rowNumber,\n  auditFlag,\n  descriptionMissing,\n  isLargeAmount,\n  requiresAudit: auditFlag !== \"None\"\n};\n"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        624,
        -96
      ],
      "id": "7096649a-d1c4-4940-ab2f-65477b33c89a",
      "name": "Code - Pre-Screen for Edge Cases"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a certified public accountant and financial data analyst specializing in startup bookkeeping. Your job is to analyze raw bank transaction descriptions and assign them to the correct Chart of Accounts category.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object. No explanation. No markdown. No code fences. Just the raw JSON.\n\nThe JSON must follow this exact structure:\n{\n  \"category\": \"one of the exact category names listed below\",\n  \"confidenceScore\": number between 0 and 100,\n  \"reasoning\": \"one to two sentences explaining your categorization decision\",\n  \"alternativeCategory\": \"second most likely category or null if confident\",\n  \"categoryCode\": \"short code as listed below\"\n}\n\nCHART OF ACCOUNTS — ALLOWED CATEGORIES (use exact names):\n- Professional Fees [code: PROF] — lawyers, accountants, consultants, freelancers, advisory services\n- Software/SaaS [code: SOFT] — Zoom, Slack, GitHub, AWS, Azure, Google Workspace, Salesforce, any subscription software\n- Travel & Entertainment [code: TRAV] — airlines, hotels, Uber, Lyft, restaurants, client meals, conferences\n- Utilities [code: UTIL] — electricity, gas, internet, phone bills, water\n- Payroll & Wages [code: PYRL] — Gusto, ADP, direct payroll transfers, contractor payments, Rippling\n- Office Supplies [code: OFFC] — Staples, Amazon (office items), paper, ink, printer supplies\n- Marketing & Advertising [code: MKTG] — Google Ads, Facebook Ads, Mailchimp, Canva, HubSpot, PR agencies\n- Bank Fees & Interest [code: BANK] — bank service charges, wire transfer fees, overdraft fees, interest charges\n- Rent & Facilities [code: RENT] — office rent, coworking spaces, WeWork, storage units, building maintenance\n- Uncategorized [code: UNCAT] — use ONLY when you genuinely cannot determine the category from the information provided\n\nCONFIDENCE SCORE RULES:\n- 90-100: Vendor name and description make the category completely unambiguous\n- 75-89: Strong indicator but some ambiguity exists\n- 50-74: Plausible guess but description is vague or vendor is unknown\n- Below 50: Very uncertain — description is too cryptic to categorize reliably\n- If description is missing and only vendor name is available, cap confidence at 70 maximum\n\nREASONING RULES:\n- Explain what specific words or patterns in the vendor name or description led to your decision\n- If using alternativeCategory, explain why it was considered\n- Be specific — mention the actual vendor name or keywords you used\n- Maximum two sentences\n\nTransaction to categorize:\nTransaction ID: {{ $json.transactionId }}\nVendor Name: {{ $json.vendorName }}\nAmount: ${{ $json.amount }}\nDescription: {{ $json.descriptionForAI }}\nCurrent Label (for reference only): {{ $json.currentLabel }}\nAudit Flag: {{ $json.auditFlag }}\n",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
